    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing a fetchland before Mishra's Bauble on turn 1. Bauble is a free 0-mana artifact that should be deployed first - it provides information (look at top card) that can inform fetch decisions, and sacrificing it puts an artifact in the graveyard contributing toward delirium for Violent Urge. There's no reason to sequence the land first.",
      "action_taken": "Played Wooded Foothills as the first action of the turn",
      "better_line": "Play Mishra's Bauble first (free), activate it targeting yourself or opponent, then play a fetchland and decide whether to crack it based on information gained",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 3,
      "player": "Llama4 Valley",
      "decision_index": 4,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Mishra's Bauble before fetching with Wooded Foothills is slightly suboptimal sequencing. If you fetch first, you shuffle your library, then Bauble lets you look at the top card of the new library (or opponent's). If you Bauble first targeting yourself, then fetch, the shuffle negates the information gained. However, targeting the opponent's library makes the order irrelevant. More importantly, fetching first would let you play Preordain this turn (fetching a blue source), giving you actual card selection rather than just a delayed draw. With Preordain in hand and no blue mana, the priority should be fetching a Steam Vents or similar blue-producing land to cast Preordain this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Mishra's Bauble before activating Wooded Foothills",
      "better_line": "Activate Wooded Foothills first to fetch a land that produces blue mana (if available), then cast Preordain for card selection, then play Mishra's Bauble with remaining priority",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 4,
      "player": "Llama4 Valley",
      "decision_index": 5,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Fetching basic Mountain instead of Steam Vents means they cannot cast Preordain on turn 1. Preordain is best cast early to find threats and set up draws. With Steam Vents, they could cast Preordain immediately this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched basic Mountain from Wooded Foothills",
      "better_line": "Fetch Steam Vents (paying 2 life to enter untapped) to have access to blue mana and cast Preordain this turn",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 6,
