    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Playing Flooded Strand at 5 life against a burn deck means paying 1 life to crack it later (going to 4), which is dangerous. Island from hand would provide the same mana without life cost. However, Flooded Strand does have upside: it can fetch different colors later, triggers Wan Shi Tong if cast later, and provides deck thinning. The Wan Shi Tong synergy (opponent searching gives counters/cards, but this is YOUR fetch) doesn't apply. At 5 life against a burn deck with Lightning Bolts, every point matters - Island would be safer while still enabling the same plays this turn.",
