    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cling to Dust exiles a card from a graveyard. If it's a creature card, you gain 3 life; otherwise, you draw a card. At 5 life against a burn/prowess deck, gaining 3 life by exiling the Slickshot Show-Off (the only creature in either graveyard) would be significantly more valuable than drawing a card by exiling Lightning Bolt. Lightning Bolt has no recursion potential from the graveyard in their deck, but the 3 life could be the difference between surviving another turn. Additionally, Slickshot Show-Off is arguably the more dangerous card if the opponent had any graveyard recursion.",
